sukhmansaran (external):I investigated this issue and can confirm it is caused by a tokenizer pipeline mismatch introduced when the tokenizer is re-saved in transformers v5. ### Root cause The original DeepSeek tokenizer uses a ByteLevel-based pipeline: - pre_tokenizer: `Sequence(Split..., ByteLevel)` - decoder: `ByteLevel` - post_processor: `TemplateProcessing` (with BOS token) However, in transformers v5 this gets replaced with: - pre_tokenizer: `Metaspace(split=False)` - decoder: `Sequence(Replace + ByteFallback + Fuse + Strip)` - post_processor: changed to `ByteLevel` This change is incompatible with the existing vocabulary. Specifically, the vocab does **not** contain metaspace-prefixed tokens: - `'How'` → valid token - `'▁How'` → not in vocab Because of this, spaces are never encoded in the token stream, and the decoder cannot reconstruct them, leading to outputs like: Howareyoudoing? ### Why decoder-only fixes don’t work This is not just a decoding issue. Since the metaspace pre-tokenizer never produces tokens aligned with the vocab, the whitespace information is already lost before decoding. Any decoder-level fix will be insufficient. ### Fix Restoring the original ByteLevel pipeline resolves the issue completely. The required changes are: - Restore pre_tokenizer to `Sequence(Split..., ByteLevel)` - Restore decoder to `ByteLevel` - Restore `TemplateProcessing` (BOS handling) After applying this, decoding becomes lossless again: decode(encode(text)) ==text across: - punctuation - whitespace - mixed inputs ### Minimal patch ```python from tokenizers import Regex from tokenizers.pre_tokenizers import Sequence, Split, ByteLevel as BLPreTok from tokenizers.processors import TemplateProcessing from tokenizers.decoders import ByteLevel as BLDecoder def fix_deepseek_tokenizer(tokenizer): backend = tokenizer.backend_tokenizer backend.pre_tokenizer = Sequence([ Split(pattern=Regex(r"\p{N}{1,3}"), behavior="isolated"), Split(pattern=Regex(r"[一-龥぀-ゟ゠-ヿ]+"), behavior="isolated"), Split( pattern=Regex( r"""[!"#$%&'()*+,\-./:;<=>?@\[\\]^_`{|}~][A-Za-z]+""" r"""|[^
\p{L}\p{P}\p{S}]?[\p{L}\p{M}]+""" r"""| ?[\p{P}\p{S}]+[
]*""" r"""|\s*[
]+""" r"""|\s+(?!\S)""" r"""|\s+""" ), behavior="isolated", ), BLPreTok(add_prefix_space=False, trim_offsets=True, use_regex=False), ]) bos = "<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>" bos_id = tokenizer.convert_tokens_to_ids(bos) backend.post_processor = TemplateProcessing( single=f"{bos}:0 $A:0", pair=f"{bos}:0 $A:0 {bos}:1 $B:1", special_tokens=[(bos, bos_id)], ) backend.decoder = BLDecoder( add_prefix_space=True, trim_offsets=True, use_regex=True, ) return tokenizer ### Result With this fix applied: - decode(encode(text)) matches the original input (modulo BOS token) - behavior matches transformers v4 and the original tokenizer.json
